# A Mac thread whose agent answered but left work running there (a build, a copy) is at work, not idle (Boss,
# 2026-10-24: a build left running made its session look idle). The unit test covers the states; this is the look.
[phone] Ask a Mac Pro thread to run something long in the background (e.g. "run sleep 120 in the background and tell me when it ends"): once it answers, its tile and tab keep a green dot and read "running on the Mac: …", not "done" or idle.
[phone] When the background work ends and the agent reports it, the thread goes back to resting (grey, "done").

# External runner turns must not need a local unfinished task or opening their tab.
[phone] After promotion, using an approved spare runner thread (include a second host such as MG1), start and stop a harmless turn outside Soma via the runner API. Leave Soma on another tab; verify no local unfinished task remains. Start another turn outside Soma that asks for a harmless approval. Without opening its thread or manually refreshing, require the approval card and notification to surface within the next periodic list refresh (foreground idle poll 30s; background idle backoff 1/2/4/5 minutes; active poll 15s, plus runner/network time). Record actual delay; do not approve it automatically.
[phone] After Boss answers the spare approval, verify pending clears and the next externally started approval also surfaces; repeated opening of Soma must not create duplicate cards/notifications or duplicate followers. Check a briefly unreachable host recovers on discovery without obscuring approvals on reachable hosts. If no safe spare host or Boss approval to run the test, mark NOT WALKED.

[phone] Battery/backoff check after promotion: with no working threads/pending approvals and Soma off screen, verify list-request intervals back off 1, 2, 4, then 5 minutes (cap). Reopen Soma: immediate list refresh, then idle foreground polls no faster than every 30s. Open Threads: immediate refresh. Start work or leave an approval pending: periodic refresh becomes 15s; when idle/background again, backoff resets to 1 minute. No duplicate watchers after repeated foreground transitions.
